\\mathbf{i}-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}?$"] [17592186372069 "Which of the following is a stream function for the vector field\n$\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=3({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-6xy\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}?$"] [17592186372076 "Which of the following is a stream function for the vector field\n$\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}(xy)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-x\\operatorname{sin}(xy)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}?$"] [17592186372083 "Which of the following is a stream function for the vector field\n$\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=2xy\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}?$"] [17592186372146 "![](images/12/12ceba806a353e10511083eb9bd29dde9b222ed8794b314057d27ef52fdf17b3.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ shown above. Which of the following shows the streamlines of this vector field?"] [17592186372181 "Determine the equation of the streamline that passes through the point $P(0,\\pi )$ for the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.$"] [17592186372209 "Let $S$ be an oriented piecewise-smooth surface bounded by the closed curve $C$ with positive orientation and parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\mathbf{k}$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$\nGiven that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=z\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+3x\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+2{y}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k},$ evaluate the integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\text{curl}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}.\n$$"] [17592186372216 "Let $S$ be an oriented piecewise-smooth surface bounded by the closed curve $C$ with positive orientation and parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+(1-\\operatorname{sin}t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$\nGiven that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=(y-z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(z-x)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+(x-y)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k},$ evaluate the integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\text{curl}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}.\n$$"] [17592186373118 "If $\\mathbf{f}(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}u \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}u \\\\ {e}^{u}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=4t-3,$ then $(\\mathbf{f}∘u)^{'}(t)=$"] [17592186373223 "Find the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf{r}(t)=⟨2-{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{t}^{2}+4,\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=4.$"] [17592186373230 "Find the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf{r}(t)=⟨\\frac{4-\\sqrt{3}{t}^{2}}{\\sqrt{2}},\\hspace{0.222em}{t}^{3},\\hspace{0.222em}t+5⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=5.$"] [17592186373757 "At which points on the curve $2{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}=-y$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{j}?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked."] [17592186373909 "Using the change of variables $u=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}$ and $v=xy,$ evaluate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}xy\\,dx\\,dy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\hspace{0.167em}:\\hspace{0.167em}{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 4{x}^{2},\\hspace{0.167em}1\\le xy\\le 5\\}.$"] [17592186373944 "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{e}^{{x}^{2}+x+y}\\,dxdy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le x\\le 1,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le y+{x}^{2}\\le 2\\}.$"] [17592186373965 "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨z+x,\\hspace{0.222em}y+2z,\\hspace{0.222em}x-4y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2x-4y$ for $-2\\le x\\le 0$ and $-1\\le y\\le 5.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{5}\\enclose{box}{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186373972 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨y,\\hspace{0.222em}x+z,\\hspace{0.222em}z+2x⟩\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=y-2x$ for $1\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$"] [17592186373979 "For a surface $S$ given by $y=h(x,z)$ for $(x,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\hspace{0.222em}Q,\\hspace{0.222em}R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={∬}_{D}(\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\hspace{0.167em}\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}+Q-R\\hspace{0.167em}\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?\n\n*Hint: The orientation of $S$ should be chosen such that the unit normal vector has a positive  $\\mathbf{j}$-component.*"] [17592186373986 "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨2x-z,\\hspace{0.222em}y-z,\\hspace{0.222em}z+y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=4x-y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ through $S$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\enclose{box}{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186374083 "Consider the finite region $R$ in the $xyz$-space, given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.222em}:\\hspace{0.222em}1\\le x+y\\le 2,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le y-x\\le 1,\\hspace{0.222em}0\\le z\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nGiven the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x+y,\\,v=y-x,\\,w=z,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2(x+y){e}^{y-x}\\,dV={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,dw\\,dv\\,du\n$$"] [17592186374090 "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu={x}^{2}+2y,\\,v=x-z,\\,w=z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$